            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0183" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5017/12–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Donnelly</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-28T19:00:00-03:00">December 28,
                            1944—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4551. Department’s circular, December 21, 10 p.m.; my 4534, December 26, 8 p.m.
                    Souza Costa said to me today “You must help me out of the coffee crisis”. I told
                    him again that our Government will not increase coffee price ceilings to which
                    he remarked “Then I will probably go to Washington to discuss the matter with
                    officials there”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donnelly</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
